>> title Meanwhile, in Lanka / The Ashoka Grove, His Side
He shows her everything. The halls, the gardens, the treasury, the women who were queens before she came.
>> pose ravana give
RAVANA: All of it is yours. I will be your servant, I who have never been anyone's. What is a man in bark cloth beside this?
>> prop grass grassBlade at 0.5
She picks a blade of grass and lays it on the ground between them. She speaks to the grass.
SITA: I am another man's wife. Tell him that the sun does not leave its light. Tell him to send me back while he still has a city.
>> pose ravana stand
>> heads \{"voices":\["desire","honour","anger","king"\],"lines":\{"desire":"l2.7","honour":"l2.8","anger":"l2.9","king":"l2.10"\}\}
He could kill her. He cannot touch her. There is an old curse on him: if he ever again takes a woman against her will, his heads will split.
RAVANA: You have twelve months to learn sense. Take her to the Ashoka grove. Guard her. Frighten her, if it helps.
>> exit sita to right in 1.6
>> enter mandodari from left to 0.1 in 1.4
From a high window, Mandodari watches the girl led away. She says nothing. She has been married to him a long time.
-> END
